/*!
\page page_stetrhitcollection StEtrHitCollection — Collection Documentation

\section etr_overview Overview

\ref StEtrHitCollection is the event-level container for hits from the
<b>ETR (Endcap Tracking prototype)</b> detector.  The ETR was a prototype
silicon-strip tracker studied for potential installation in the STAR endcap.

Its geometry comprises <b>3 radial layers</b> and <b>12 azimuthal sectors</b>.
Each \ref StEtrHit carries a 3-D position, sector (0–11), layer (0–2), pad
section (0–29), and deposited charge.  \c addHit enforces valid layer and sector
indices via \c assert.

\section etr_ownership Object Ownership

<b>mHits</b> (\c StSPtrVecEtrHit): <b>Owned</b>; elements deleted by \c StSPtrVec.
The \ref StEtrHitCollection destructor is a <b>no-op</b>.  The collection itself
is owned by the \c StEvent framework.

\section etr_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StSPtrVecEtrHit | mHits | Collection of \ref StEtrHit objects with position, sector (0–11), layer (0–2), section (0–29), and charge. |

Internal geometry constants (private enums):

| Constant | Value |
|----------|-------|
| \c mNumberOfLayers | 3 |
| \c mNumberOfSectors | 12 |

\section etr_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c hits() | Reference to the hit collection (mutable and const overloads). |
| \c addHit(StEtrHit*) | Appends a hit; \c assert checks layer < 3 and sector < 12. Returns \c kTRUE on success. |
| \c numberOfHits() const | Total number of hits in the collection. |
| \c numberOfLayers() const | Returns 3. |
| \c numberOfSectors() const | Returns 12. |

\section etr_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StEtrHitCollection* etrColl = event->etrHitCollection();
if (!etrColl || etrColl->numberOfHits() == 0) return;

const StSPtrVecEtrHit& hits = etrColl->hits();
for (size_t i = 0; i < hits.size(); ++i) {
    StEtrHit* hit = hits[i];
    int   layer   = hit->layer();    // 0-2
    int   sector  = hit->sector();   // 0-11
    int   section = hit->section();  // 0-29
    float charge  = hit->charge();
}
\endcode

\see StEtrHit
*/
